# ENV REGISTER: annotations on settings dev.env sets, never a substitute for setting one.
# The rule (owner, 2026-11-23): no setting may be unset. Every setting the served table has is set in
# dev.env at a stated value, and choosing the engine default means writing that default out with its
# read site. A rebase that adds a row fails check-env-coverage.py until its value is written in dev.env
# and the worklist line this script added is deleted. A `# missing NAME=` line is temporary work,
# never a resting state; a `# default-ok|debt|unreachable NAME:` line annotates a value that is already
# set and must cite its evidence. A `# image-baked NAME=value:` line records that the served image's own
# ENV carries the name, which forbids the `unset` form: the container always has a value.
# The production engine's verdicts are the `# prod <kind> NAME:` block at the end, read with
# check-env-coverage.py --tag prod; the untagged lines above are the dev arm's, and the two runs ignore
# each other. The production record is prod.env and its derived table is docs/receipts/ProdEnvAudit/.

# image-baked TENSORFOLD_CUDA_KERNELS=/opt/tensorfold/share/tensorfold/cuda/sm121: both r5 images carry it in their own ENV, so `unset` cannot reach the container and dev.env states the value instead. Evidence: docs/KNOB-SCREEN.md, work/EnvBoot/RESULT.md.
# debt TENSORFOLD_CUDA_KERNELS: the choice of native over a captured set is unmeasured on this stack (A3); every measured receipt here ran native, and a captured set is inadmissible at the fp8 shape. Evidence: docs/KNOB-COVERAGE.md.
# absent TF_ROCE_GID_INDEX: dev.env states it as `unset`, and absence is the decision: cuda/roce.zig:255 searches the GID table only when the variable is null, and any text (blank included) names an index the verbs path parses (roce_verbs.zig:148); arm A's container env carries 30 serve names and not this one (work/QRerun/box/out/QA/env.txt). evidence work/DevTree/zig/src/cuda/roce.zig:255

# --- The INT4 port's four rows (patches/main-1ece6e6db-r5-dev/0021): two carry production's own served values and two
# are the engine's defaults, each stated in dev.env with its read site. They are not "absent from the dev tree": 0021
# adds all four to the table (zig/src/platform/environment.zig:84-87) and reads them in
# zig/src/families/flashnext/cuda_int4.zig. Evidence: docs/INT4-PORT.md, work/DevEnvComp/READERS.md.
# measured TF_FLASHNEXT_HEAD_ROW_TILES: set 2, production's serve value (the head's calls past 16 rows take 32-row items, cuda_int4.zig:432) read in every exactness cell. Evidence: docs/receipts/QInt4/RESULT.md, docs/INT4-PORT.md.
# measured TF_FLASHNEXT_INT4_PROMPT_GATE_UP: set 1, production's serve value (int4_prompt_kernel for the routed gate/up, cuda_int4.zig:272-273) read in every exactness cell. Evidence: docs/receipts/QInt4/RESULT.md, docs/INT4-PORT.md.
# debt TF_FLASHNEXT_INT4_TILE: set 16, the engine's own default keeps 16-pair items (cuda_int4.zig:151-152); 64 is unmeasured on this stack. Evidence: work/DevEnvComp/READERS.md.
# debt TF_FLASHNEXT_INT4_PROMPT_DOWN: set 1, the engine's own default keeps the prompt down on (cuda_int4.zig:386-387); 0 is unmeasured on this stack. Evidence: work/DevEnvComp/READERS.md.
# raw TF_FLASHNEXT_MTP_WEIGHTS: read through a raw getenv (zig/src/families/flashnext/cuda_mtp_mxfp8.zig:23), so it has no table row; dev.env leaves it out and the dev launcher sets mxfp8 by default (the INT4 drafter arm's value, scripts/qwen38/zig/qwen6-start.sh), a debt until its own r5 A/B. Evidence: docs/INT4-PORT.md, work/DevEnvComp/READERS.md.

