# --- DEV ARM: one verdict on every dev.env row (PROMOTION-RULES.md, one verdict a row)
# Each line annotates the value dev.env states, in dev.env's own order. Kinds are the rule's (measured,
# inert, debt, raw, launcher, absent, candidate, retired) plus the legacy default-ok and unreachable the
# checker still accepts. Evidence is the dev tree the table is measured against (work/DevTree, upstream
# 1ece6e6d + patches/main-1ece6e6db-r5-dev) or the file that records a search.
# inert TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB: 10 matches production's launcher; the reserve measured level in every cell and is an admission bound, not a speed arm (docs/KNOB-COVERAGE.md, never-sweep list), evidence work/DevTree/zig/src/native/cuda_family_memory.zig:39
# launcher TENSORFOLD_NO_UPDATE_CHECK: no engine reader: the dev launcher states it in its exec env and the tree's benchmark server sets it for its child, so the update check is a launcher concern, evidence scripts/qwen38/zig/qwen6-start.sh:80
# inert TENSORFOLD_VIDEO_TOKENS: the vision input budget; the dev launcher serves with VISION=0, so the media path this bounds does not run, evidence work/DevTree/zig/src/server/vision_inputs.zig:301
# debt TF_FLASHNEXT_BATCH_DRAWS: the engine's own default 1; A1 worklist row 5 (batched against per-stream draws) has no cells, evidence work/DevTree/zig/src/families/flashnext/cuda_draw_batch.zig:18
# debt TF_FLASHNEXT_CONFIDENCE: production's -0.15 for this checkpoint; the dev cells put -0.20 level and 0 slower, and the engine default -0.4 has no cell here, evidence work/DevTree/zig/src/families/flashnext/cuda_lanes_load.zig:94
# launcher TF_FLASHNEXT_DEPTH: no engine reader in the dev tree (only the DEPTH_LOG diagnostic); the dev launcher's exec env states 15 for the production engine's parity, evidence scripts/qwen38/zig/qwen6-start.sh:84
# launcher TF_FLASHNEXT_WINDOW: no engine reader in the dev tree (the only WINDOW spellings are WINDOW_CHECK, WINDOW_GRAPH and WINDOW_ROWS); the dev launcher states 64 for parity, evidence scripts/qwen38/zig/qwen6-start.sh:93
# launcher TENSORFOLD_VISION_PYTHONPATH: no engine reader anywhere in the dev tree: a vision launcher convention, not an engine setting, evidence docs/ENV-REGISTER.md:204
